Subject: [PATCH 417/488] [DS4.1] Per-request row scatters in TileLang

The runner committed a step's drafts with two torch index ops (into the
request states, then read back for the next step), and adaptive
verification scattered the drafts' confidences with a third. One
TileLang scatter, read back in the same launch where the runner needs
the rows, replaces each; a negative index wraps as torch's indexing does.
The boundary checkpoint's replayed drafts take the same kernel. Tested
bit for bit against torch's indexing.
